From c3a0cb1efc08dca08f890dac278195f1d86e7690 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yomi Session <kurotech@yomi.local>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 03:39:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] fix(remediator): #14 critical-PID protection, #15 path
 containment (not startswith)

All 4 pre-Fase-6 mandatory gates now FIXED: #12, #13, #14, #15, #21.

#14: _validate_payload now rejects pid<=100, mirroring harness.py's
hardblock. Deliberately skips harness.py's psutil-based NoSuchProcess
fail-safe check -- remediator.py's design intent is to keep generating
rollback scripts for self-deleted (fileless) malware PIDs, so failing
safe on a missing PID would defeat that purpose.

#15: critical system path check now uses real pathlib containment
(resolved path == critical dir, or critical dir in resolved.parents)
instead of exact string match against bare directory names. Explicitly
NOT implemented via .startswith() -- that would repeat the exact bug
class already flagged for mirage.py (known_issues.md #16/#18):
startswith('/etc') also wrongly matches /etcetera/file. '/' stays as
exact-match only (not containment), since containment against '/'
would mean every absolute path is 'under' it.

6 new tests replace the 2 old KNOWN_GAP tests in test_remediator.py
(regression tests for the fix, not just skipped).

Verified: 452/452 unit passed (root), 451 passed + 1 skipped as
non-root, stable across 5 runs. Lint clean. 5 integration + 1 benchmark
test passed (run separately -- full run_tests.sh hit a sandbox tooling
timeout, not a code issue).

Also updates docs/known_issues.md (#14, #15 -> FIXED), docs/phase_log/
fase_5.md and README.md (now covers all 4 gates, not 3), and
scripts/create_known_issues_fase5.sh (now also closes GH #16/#17 for
remediator.py, confirmed numbers from the actual GitHub issues
screenshot rather than guessed).
